# [MODULE DOC]
# Tempita template generating _kd_tree.pyx. It instantiates, for float64
# (suffix 64) and float32 (suffix 32) inputs, the KDTree specialization of
# the generic BinaryTree defined in _binary_tree.pxi (included textually).
# Each node is an axis-aligned bounding box: node_bounds[0, i_node] holds the
# per-feature minima and node_bounds[1, i_node] the maxima of the node's
# points. The module-level hooks (allocate_data, init_node, min/max(r)dist and
# dual-tree variants) are called by name from _binary_tree.pxi. Bounds are
# computed for Minkowski-type metrics only (euclidean, manhattan, chebyshev,
# minkowski with parameter p), using the metric's p (INF for chebyshev).
# The public KDTree is the float64 class.
